    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:authorConclusion",
      "object": "Socially prescribed perfectionism did not explain variance in dietary restraint scores. Self esteem oriented perfectionism was associated with dietary restraint and was related to body dissatisfaction. The current findings show a mediating effect of body esteem weight satisfaction on the relationship between self-oriented perfectionism and dietary restraint. The perfectionist personality would be a contributing factor in dietary restraint required to maintin a low body weight."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:limites",
      "object": "Limitations of the study were linked to self-report measures and the cross-sectional nature of the investigations."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:perspectives",
      "object": "Future research is needed to gain a fuller understanding of the relationship between these three variable. The use of both self-report measures and interview formats in longitudinal studies must be developed to gain a more precise estimate of the nature and extent of inappropriate compensatory behaviours amog synchronized swimmers."
    },
